# config/approval-notify - opt-in notification when a decision is newly held for
# the captain (bin/fm-captain-hold.sh hold). Copy this into a local, gitignored
# config/approval-notify and edit. One directive per non-empty, non-comment line.
# An absent or empty file sends nothing.
#
# Directives:
#   off              position-independent kill switch
#   command:<cmd>    run <cmd> via `sh -c`; the message is passed as $1 and on
#                    stdin, so it can reach a phone or pager
#
# The message is "Approval needed: <task title> [<task id>]" plus a verified pull
# request link when the task records one. The hold reason and backlog notes are
# never sent. This only announces that a decision is waiting; answer it in
# Firstmate as usual.
#
# Example: push to a phone through ntfy.sh. Replace the topic with your own
# private topic, and treat anyone who knows it as able to read these messages.
command: curl --fail --silent --show-error --max-time 8 -H "Title: Firstmate approval needed" --data-binary "$1" "https://ntfy.sh/replace-with-your-topic"
